            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous radiofrequency glossopharyngeal rhizotomy for cancer pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>154-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>15 patients with pain secondary to cancer underwent radiofrequency glossopharyngeal rhizotomy by the percutaneous approach. 11 patients had complete relief while 4 patients had partial relief. All patients presented, after surgery, some impairment in glossopharyngeal function.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
